WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.1 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
MEAL principles and a proportionate system

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
MEAL tells you, from day one, whether you are doing what you said and what to change.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
MEAL stands for Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Learning. It is a light system that tells you whether you are doing what you said, whether it makes a difference and what to change.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Four parts, four questions

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.241
Monitoring: Tracks, regularly, what you are doing and what is changing. For example: A sheet filled in every Saturday: loaves sold, loaves left over and who attended.

6
00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:48.089
Evaluation: Asks whether it made a difference, for whom and why. For example: A short end-of-pilot review: did trainees finish, and are they finding work?

7
00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:59.419
Accountability: The people you serve can shape the work and raise concerns safely. For example: A feedback card at the stall, plus a trusted youth-centre contact for sensitive concerns.

8
00:00:59.419 --> 00:01:11.948
Learning: Turns what you found into decisions for the next round. For example: After the pilot, three decisions: new shift times, another café buyer, a search for a shop.

9
00:01:12.348 --> 00:01:12.948
Why start it now

10
00:01:12.948 --> 00:01:18.622
1. You have evidence from day one instead of reconstructing it later.

11
00:01:18.622 --> 00:01:24.296
2. You find out early whether your idea works, before you grow.

12
00:01:24.296 --> 00:01:30.230
3. Funders, customers and members trust results they can see.

13
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.230
What it builds

14
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.533
1. One chain: Theory of Change, results, indicators, data, learning, decisions.

15
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:42.207
2. Each lesson in this module adds one link to that chain.

16
00:01:42.207 --> 00:01:48.511
3. Your reports, proof points and communications draw on it later.

17
00:01:48.911 --> 00:01:49.511
What to avoid

18
00:01:49.511 --> 00:01:54.444
Collecting data you will never use for a decision.

19
00:01:54.444 --> 00:02:00.119
Fifty indicators nobody reviews instead of three to five good ones.

20
00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:06.793
Waiting for tablets or databases: paper sheets and photos are enough.

21
00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.193
You write your MEAL purpose and the decisions it must inform.

22
00:02:09.193 --> 00:02:13.193
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:14.693 --> 00:02:17.793
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
